%% One question: how an answer gets accepted and collected.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant R as Runner (host)
    participant S as Sandbox (pi agent)
    participant M as Model

    R->>S: docker run: page images, text layer, prompt
    S->>M: prompt + pages + tool list

    loop until answer accepted, plain-text reply, or turn cap (25)
        M-->>S: tool call
        alt zoom / bash / read / write
            S->>M: tool result (crop image or output)
        else answer
            Note right of S: validate with the baseline's normalize_response
            alt invalid, or first empty answer
                S->>M: "Rejected: reason"
            else valid
                Note right of S: write answer.json, end session
            end
        end
    end

    opt wall-clock timeout (host)
        R->>S: docker kill
    end
    S-->>R: container exits
    Note over R: re-validate answer.json
    alt valid and non-empty
        Note over R: agent answer goes into submission.xlsx
    else missing, invalid, empty or timed out
        Note over R: leave empty (or take --fallback answer)
    end
